1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,542
Did you know our

2
00:00:01,562 --> 00:00:03,860
SALARY CYCLE is changing?

3
00:00:03,940 --> 00:00:06,646
Here's what it means for you.

4
00:00:07,060 --> 00:00:09,084
Up to now, it has followed

5
00:00:09,104 --> 00:00:11,550
a JANUARY-to-DECEMBER cycle

6
00:00:11,630 --> 00:00:14,635
12 months, one cycle.

7
00:00:15,160 --> 00:00:16,093
MERIT

8
00:00:16,113 --> 00:00:20,350
Projected market salary movement

9
00:00:20,430 --> 00:00:21,561
BONUS

10
00:00:21,581 --> 00:00:25,930
Estimated company performance

11
00:00:26,010 --> 00:00:29,888
HSE  ·  FINANCE  ·  PERFORMANCE

12
00:00:30,620 --> 00:00:33,890
Now, we're moving to a new cycle.

13
00:00:33,970 --> 00:00:36,837
From APRIL to MARCH

14
00:00:37,710 --> 00:00:40,705
Merit increases and promotions

15
00:00:40,725 --> 00:00:43,210
take effect on APRIL 1

16
00:00:43,290 --> 00:00:46,235
That's where the cycle now begins.

17
00:00:46,890 --> 00:00:47,777
BONUS

18
00:00:47,797 --> 00:00:50,910
paid in the MARCH payroll

19
00:00:50,990 --> 00:00:52,897
MARCH is the last month

20
00:00:52,917 --> 00:00:54,373
of the cycle

21
00:00:54,850 --> 00:00:57,910
One thing that isn't changing

22
00:00:57,990 --> 00:00:59,878
Your PERFORMANCE APPRAISAL

23
00:00:59,899 --> 00:01:01,940
stays on the same schedule

24
00:01:02,020 --> 00:01:04,058
and it will still close

25
00:01:04,078 --> 00:01:05,512
in DECEMBER

26
00:01:06,360 --> 00:01:09,190
One more thing worth knowing

27
00:01:09,270 --> 00:01:13,040
Say your merit increase is 5%

28
00:01:13,120 --> 00:01:16,275
The implementation year covers

29
00:01:16,295 --> 00:01:19,050
15 MONTHS instead of 12

30
00:01:19,130 --> 00:01:23,049
5% ÷ 12 = about 0.417%

31
00:01:23,069 --> 00:01:24,900
per month

32
00:01:24,980 --> 00:01:28,540
Multiply that by 15 months

33
00:01:28,620 --> 00:01:32,030
and the equivalent becomes

34
00:01:32,050 --> 00:01:33,555
6.25%

35
00:01:34,310 --> 00:01:37,130
APRIL to MARCH

36
00:01:37,210 --> 00:01:39,861
That's the one to remember.

37
00:01:40,620 --> 00:01:42,650
Why the change?

38
00:01:42,730 --> 00:01:46,020
Closer to market best practice

39
00:01:46,100 --> 00:01:48,274
More relevant information

40
00:01:48,294 --> 00:01:50,499
when we set salaries

41
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:53,090
If you have questions,

42
00:01:53,170 --> 00:01:55,944
HR is ready to help.
